# The `_calendar` stack is the subscription: while it exists, every
# committed client mutation in this tenant's calendars (put, delete,
# mkcalendar, remove, proppatch — where the calendar's policy says
# observe) arrives here with @calendar.phase == "observe", after the
# client already got its reply. Facts ride under @calendar.*: op,
# calendar{id,name,display_name,timezone}, object{name,uid,etag,…}, the
# object's iCalendar text at @calendar.ical and its parse at
# @calendar.event (start_utc, recur{freq,…}, …). This rule just records
# what it saw; a product would reconcile @calendar.event into its own
# canonical state.
WHEN @calendar.phase == "observe"
  EMIT ._observed = &object(
         "op", @calendar.op,
         "calendar", @calendar.calendar.name,
         "uid", @calendar.object.uid,
         "summary", @calendar.event.summary)
